          {
            "title": "Intro",
            "id": 115251,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Às vezes, precisamos converter uma série de valores de um array em um único valor. Por exemplo, quando queremos calcular uma soma.</p><p>Uma maneira clássica de fazer isso é através de um loop.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" miles = [\" /><text value=\"33\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"95\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"79\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" total = \" /><text value=\"0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"for\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" (\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" element \" /><text value=\"of\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" miles) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" total += element;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(total);\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"75\" endIndex=\"80\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"207\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Certifique-se de escolher <code>total</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Às vezes, precisamos converter uma série de valores de um array em um único valor. Por exemplo, quando queremos calcular uma soma.</p><p>Uma forma clássica é usar um loop. Complete a atualização do total para o código exibir <code>207</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" miles = [\" /><text value=\"33\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"95\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"79\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"let\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" total = \" /><text value=\"0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\";\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"for\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" (\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" element \" /><text value=\"of\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" miles) {\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" total += element;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"}\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(total);\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"75\" endIndex=\"80\" /><option startIndex=\"81\" endIndex=\"83\" /><option startIndex=\"54\" endIndex=\"61\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"miles\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"-=\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"index\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"207\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Certifique-se de escolher <code>element</code> seguido de <code>total</code> e finalmente <code>+=</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Calling .reduce on an Array",
            "id": 115252,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>No entanto, JavaScript oferece um método mais simples e já existente. <code>.reduce()</code> pode combinar valores de um Array em um valor usando uma função inline.</p><p><code>.reduce()</code> usa a sintaxe: <code>ArrayName.reduce()</code>. Vamos ver como poderíamos chamá-lo no array <code>miles</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" miles = [\" /><text value=\"33\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"95\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"79\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" total = miles.reduce();\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"42\" endIndex=\"47\" /><option startIndex=\"47\" endIndex=\"48\" /><option startIndex=\"48\" endIndex=\"54\" /><option startIndex=\"54\" endIndex=\"55\" /><option startIndex=\"55\" endIndex=\"56\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"list\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"        \" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Certifique-se de escolher <code>miles</code> seguido de <code>.</code> e depois <code>reduce</code>, <code>(</code>, <code>)</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>No entanto, JavaScript oferece um método mais simples e já existente. <code>.reduce()</code> pode combinar valores de um Array em um valor usando uma função inline.</p><p><code>.reduce()</code> usa a sintaxe <code>ArrayName.reduce()</code>. Crie essa chamada em <code>miles</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" miles = [\" /><text value=\"33\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"95\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"79\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" total = miles.reduce();\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"42\" endIndex=\"47\" /><option startIndex=\"47\" endIndex=\"48\" /><option startIndex=\"48\" endIndex=\"54\" /><option startIndex=\"54\" endIndex=\"55\" /><option startIndex=\"55\" endIndex=\"56\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"map\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"filter\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"push\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Certifique-se de escolher <code>miles</code> seguido de <code>.</code>, <code>reduce</code>, <code>(</code> e finalmente <code>)</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Passing Functions",
            "id": 115253,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Para informar à função <code>.reduce()</code> como combinar valores, primeiro precisamos passar uma função como parâmetro.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" miles = [\" /><text value=\"33\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"95\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"79\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" total = miles.reduce(\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{});\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"55\" endIndex=\"63\" /><option startIndex=\"63\" endIndex=\"64\" /><option startIndex=\"64\" endIndex=\"65\" /><option startIndex=\"66\" endIndex=\"67\" /><option startIndex=\"67\" endIndex=\"68\" /></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Certifique-se de escolher <code>function</code> seguido de <code>(</code> e depois <code>)</code>, <code>{</code>, <code>}</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Para informar à função <code>.reduce()</code> como combinar valores, primeiro precisamos passar uma função como parâmetro.</p><p>Complete o callback vazio recebido por <code>reduce()</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" miles = [\" /><text value=\"33\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"95\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"79\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" total = miles.reduce(\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{});\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"55\" endIndex=\"63\" /><option startIndex=\"63\" endIndex=\"64\" /><option startIndex=\"64\" endIndex=\"65\" /><option startIndex=\"66\" endIndex=\"67\" /><option startIndex=\"67\" endIndex=\"68\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"=&gt;\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"[\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"]\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Certifique-se de escolher <code>function</code> seguido de <code>(</code>, <code>)</code>, <code>{</code> e finalmente <code>}</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Parameters",
            "id": 115255,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Nossa função precisa de dois parâmetros: o primeiro para acessar o resultado da <strong>redução</strong> anterior, e o segundo para acessar o valor atual.</p><p>Adicione dois parâmetros: <code>prev</code> e <code>curr</code>, nessa ordem.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" miles = [\" /><text value=\"33\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"95\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"79\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" total = miles.reduce(\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"prev, curr\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{});\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"64\" endIndex=\"69\" /><option startIndex=\"70\" endIndex=\"74\" /></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Certifique-se de escolher <code>prev,</code> seguido de <code>curr</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Return",
            "id": 115254,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p><code>reduce()</code> itera através de um array e, em cada valor, realiza uma operação com os dois parâmetros até chegar a um único valor.</p><p>Por exemplo, para somar os valores, a função inline retorna a soma da redução de <code>prev</code> e o valor <code>curr</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" miles = [\" /><text value=\"33\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"95\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"79\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" total = miles.reduce(\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"prev, curr\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" prev + curr;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"});\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(total);\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"79\" endIndex=\"85\" /><option startIndex=\"86\" endIndex=\"97\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"207\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Certifique-se de escolher <code>return</code> seguido de <code>prev + curr</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p><code>reduce()</code> itera através de um array e, em cada valor, realiza uma operação com os dois parâmetros até chegar a um único valor.</p><p>Por exemplo, para somar os valores, a função inline retorna a soma da redução de <code>prev</code> e o valor <code>curr</code>.</p><p>Nomeie o primeiro parâmetro como <code>prev</code> e o segundo como <code>curr</code>.</p><p>Complete essa instrução return para o código imprimir <code>207</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" miles = [\" /><text value=\"33\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"95\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"79\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" total = miles.reduce(\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"prev, curr\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" prev + curr;\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"});\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(total);\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"79\" endIndex=\"85\" /><option startIndex=\"64\" endIndex=\"68\" /><option startIndex=\"91\" endIndex=\"92\" /><option startIndex=\"70\" endIndex=\"74\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"-\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"*\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"total\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"207\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Certifique-se de escolher <code>prev</code> seguido de <code>curr</code>, <code>return</code> e finalmente <code>+</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Arrow functions",
            "id": 115258,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Para simplificar nossa sintaxe, podemos incorporar uma função de seta do JavaScript no lugar da função inline.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" miles = [\" /><text value=\"33\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"95\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"79\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" total = miles.reduce(\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"prevVal, currVal\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") =&gt;\" /><text value=\" prevVal + currVal);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(total);\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"55\" endIndex=\"73\" /><option startIndex=\"74\" endIndex=\"76\" /><option startIndex=\"77\" endIndex=\"94\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&lt;=\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"-\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"207\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Certifique-se de escolher <code>(prevVal, currVal)</code> seguido de <code>=&gt;</code> e finalmente <code>prevVal + currVal</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Para simplificar nossa sintaxe, podemos incorporar uma função de seta do JavaScript no lugar da função inline.</p><p>Nomeie os parâmetros como <code>prevVal</code> e <code>currVal</code>, nessa ordem.</p><p>Coloque <code>prevVal</code> à esquerda e <code>currVal</code> à direita. Escolha o operador para o total ser <code>207</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" miles = [\" /><text value=\"33\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"95\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"79\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" total = miles.reduce(\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"prevVal, currVal\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") =&gt;\" /><text value=\" prevVal + currVal);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(total);\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"56\" endIndex=\"63\" /><option startIndex=\"65\" endIndex=\"72\" /><option startIndex=\"74\" endIndex=\"76\" /><option startIndex=\"77\" endIndex=\"84\" /><option startIndex=\"85\" endIndex=\"86\" /><option startIndex=\"87\" endIndex=\"94\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"&lt;=\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"-\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"index\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"207\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Certifique-se de escolher <code>prevVal</code> seguido de <code>currVal</code>, <code>=&gt;</code>, <code>prevVal</code>, <code>+</code> e finalmente <code>currVal</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Parameters II",
            "id": 115256,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Se incluirmos um terceiro parâmetro na função, também podemos acessar o índice de cada iteração.</p><p>Neste exemplo, usamos <code>.reduce()</code> para somar os <code>prices</code>, mas também incorporamos <code>index</code> para aplicar um fator de desconto de um segundo array.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" prices = [\" /><text value=\"17.50\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"20.25\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"24.75\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"13.50\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"8.50\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" discountFactor = [\" /><text value=\"0.9\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"0.9\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"1.0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"1.0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"0.9\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" total = prices.reduce(\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"prevVal, currVal, index\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" prevVal + (currVal * discountFactor[index]);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"});\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(total);\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"156\" endIndex=\"161\" /><option startIndex=\"209\" endIndex=\"214\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"81.625\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Certifique-se de escolher <code>index</code> seguido de <code>index</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Se incluirmos um terceiro parâmetro na função, também podemos acessar o índice de cada iteração.</p><p>Neste exemplo, usamos <code>.reduce()</code> para somar <code>prices</code> e também usamos <code>index</code>.</p><p>Ele aplica um desconto de outro array. Complete a busca por índice para exibir <code>81.625</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"javascript\" name=\"script.js\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" prices = [\" /><text value=\"17.50\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"20.25\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"24.75\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"13.50\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"8.50\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" discountFactor = [\" /><text value=\"0.9\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"0.9\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"1.0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"1.0\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"0.9\" class=\"number\" /><text value=\"];\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"const\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" total = prices.reduce(\" /><text value=\"function\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"prevVal, currVal, index\" class=\"params\" /><text value=\") \" /><text value=\"{\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"return\" class=\"keyword\" /><text value=\" prevVal + (currVal * discountFactor[index]);\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"});\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"console\" class=\"built_in\" /><text value=\".log(total);\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"156\" endIndex=\"161\" /><option startIndex=\"57\" endIndex=\"71\" /><option startIndex=\"209\" endIndex=\"214\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"prices\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"prevVal\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"currVal\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"81.625\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Certifique-se de escolher <code>discountFactor</code> seguido de <code>index</code> e finalmente <code>index</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Question: Intro",
            "id": 115259,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Qual função JavaScript podemos usar para converter uma série de valores de array em um único valor?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>.reduce()</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>.filter()</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Certifique-se de escolher <code>.reduce()</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Qual função JavaScript podemos usar para converter uma série de valores de array em um único valor?</p><p>Você precisa de um total de todos os números de um array. Escolha o método criado para esse resultado.</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>.reduce()</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>.filter()</code></item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\"><code>.map()</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Certifique-se de escolher <code>.reduce()</code>.</p></body></html>"
